{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","title":"def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":870,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-group]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixC#prop:normal-covering-transitive-action]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","line":1341,"source":"\\begin{definition}\n\\label{def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive}\n\n\\uses{def:covering-automorphism-group, prop:normal-covering-transitive-action}\n\n\n\n\nThe covering $\\pi$ is \\emph{normal} if $\\operatorname{Aut}_\\pi(\\tilde M)$ acts transitively on every fiber. Equivalently, the image of $\\pi_*:\\pi_1(\\tilde M,\\tilde x)\\to\\pi_1(M,\\pi(\\tilde x))$ is normal (Proposition C.21).\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6e6f726d616c2d636f766572696e672d66696272652d7472616e736974697665\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Acovering-automorphism-group\">↗ def:covering-automorphism-group</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixC%23prop%3Anormal-covering-transitive-action\">↗ prop:normal-covering-transitive-action</a> <p></p>The covering <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span> is <em>normal</em> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Aut}_\\pi (\\tilde M)$\">$\\operatorname {Aut}_\\pi (\\tilde M)$</span> acts transitively on every fiber. Equivalently, the image of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi _*:\\pi _1(\\tilde M,\\tilde x)\\to \\pi _1(M,\\pi (\\tilde x))$\">$\\pi _*:\\pi _1(\\tilde M,\\tilde x)\\to \\pi _1(M,\\pi (\\tilde x))$</span> is normal (Proposition C.21). ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-group","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-group","title":"def:covering-automorphism-group","label":"def:covering-automorphism-group"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixC#prop:normal-covering-transitive-action","title":"prop:normal-covering-transitive-action","label":"prop:normal-covering-transitive-action"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-covering-metric","title":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric","label":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","title":"def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","tex":"\\begin{definition}\n\\label{def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive}\n\n\\uses{def:covering-automorphism-group, prop:normal-covering-transitive-action}\n\n\n\n\nThe covering $\\pi$ is \\emph{normal} if $\\operatorname{Aut}_\\pi(\\tilde M)$ acts transitively on every fiber. Equivalently, the image of $\\pi_*:\\pi_1(\\tilde M,\\tilde x)\\to\\pi_1(M,\\pi(\\tilde x))$ is normal (Proposition C.21).\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencie